### 4. Packaging Binary with App Name, Publisher & Logo

To embed the logo, application name, version, and publisher metadata directly into the standalone Go binary without external Go libraries, compile a native Windows resource object (`.syso`) using GNU `windres` (from MinGW) before `go build`, and include a `.desktop` bundle for Linux.

#### `packaging/windows/app.rc`

```rc
1 ICON "nssf.ico"

1 VERSIONINFO
FILEVERSION     1,0,0,0
PRODUCTVERSION  1,0,0,0
FILEFLAGSMASK   0x3fL
FILEFLAGS       0x0L
FILEOS          0x40004L
FILETYPE        0x1L
FILESUBTYPE     0x0L
BEGIN
    BLOCK "StringFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        BLOCK "040904b0"
        BEGIN
            VALUE "CompanyName",      "National Social Security Fund (NSSF) Kenya"
            VALUE "FileDescription",  "NSSF Member Statement Secure Dispatch Portal"
            VALUE "FileVersion",      "1.0.0.0"
            VALUE "InternalName",     "nssf-dispatch"
            VALUE "LegalCopyright",   "Copyright (C) 2026 NSSF Kenya. All rights reserved."
            VALUE "OriginalFilename", "NSSF-Statement-Dispatch.exe"
            VALUE "ProductName",      "NSSF Digital Statement Dispatcher"
            VALUE "ProductVersion",   "1.0.0.0"
        END
    END
    BLOCK "VarFileInfo"
    BEGIN
        VALUE "Translation", 0x409, 1200
    END
END

```

#### `build.sh` — Full Build & Packaging Script

```bash
#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -e

echo "[1/4] Building React TypeScript frontend..."
cd web
npm install
npm run build
cd ..

echo "[2/4] Copying dist assets into Go embed directory..."
rm -rf cmd/server/dist
cp -r web/dist cmd/server/dist

echo "[3/4] Compiling Windows PE Resource (Logo, Publisher, App Name)..."
x86_64-w64-mingw32-windres packaging/windows/app.rc -O coff -o cmd/server/rsrc_windows_amd64.syso

echo "[4/4] Building standalone single-file binaries..."
mkdir -p release

# Windows Executable (with embedded icon, publisher, app name & React UI)
GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build \
  -ldflags="-s -w -H=windowsgui" \
  -o release/NSSF-Statement-Dispatch.exe ./cmd/server

# Linux Executable
GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build \
  -ldflags="-s -w" \
  -o release/nssf-statement-dispatch-linux ./cmd/server

echo "Done! Standalone binaries created in ./release/"

```